    <DataNode elementId="MONOMER-20525" textLabel="flavonoid 3&apos;-hydroxylase/flavone 5&apos;-hydroxylase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q8LM92" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="711.765869140625" centerY="664.734375" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="SRI, caspi">Analysis of rice metabolites indicated the presence of 5&apos;-hydroxylated flavonoids. |FRAME: EC-1.14.14.81 EC 1.14.14.81, flavanoid 3&amp;prime;,5&amp;prime;-hydroxylase|, an enzyme responsible for 5&apos; hydroxylation of flavonoids, is often encoded by members of the CYP75A family. The rice genome has only a single copy of a CYP75A member, CYP75A11. However, studies of that enzyme concluded that it does not have a flavonoid 3&apos;- or 3&apos;,5&apos;-hydroxylase activities |CITS: [26082402]|. |FRAME: G-58315 CYP75B4| is a close homolog of |FRAME: G-58317 CYP75B3|, which encodes |FRAME: EC-1.14.14.81 EC 1.14.14.81, flavanoid 3&amp;prime;,5&amp;prime;-hydroxylase|. A mutation in |FRAME: G-58315 CYP75B4| results in complete absence of |FRAME: CPD-12572 tricin| derivatives. Instead, the mutant accumulated |FRAME: CPD-431 apigenin| and |FRAME: 5734-TETRAHYDROXYFLAVONE luteolin|. In addition, |FRAME: 574-TRIHYDROXY-3-METHOXYFLAVONE chrysoeriol| was detected in the mutant, but not in the wild type. Taken together, these observations suggested that the |FRAME: G-58315 CYP75B4| gene may encode a flavonoid 5&apos;-hydroxylase |CITS: [26082402]|. Complementation studies of the Arabidopsis tt7 mutants, which are defective in |FRAME: EC-1.14.14.82 EC 1.14.14.82, flavonoid 3&amp;prime;-monooxygenase|, revelaed that |FRAME: G-58315 CYP75B4| restores this defficiency. It was also found that the enzyme was only able to introduce 3&apos;-hydroxylation, but not 5&apos;-hydroxylation, to the endogenous flavonoids in Arabidopsis |CITS: [26082402]|. However, when the gene was co-expressed in Arabidopsis with the |FRAME: G-58314 CYP93G1| gene, whose product produces flavones (not naturally produced by Arabidopsis), the recombinant plants produced the 5&apos;-hydroxylated |FRAME: CPD-12571 selgin| and |FRAME: CPD-12572 tricin|, indicating that |FRAME: G-58315 CYP75B4| also has a flavone 5&apos;-hydroxylase activity. The 5&apos;-hydroxylation of |FRAME: 574-TRIHYDROXY-3-METHOXYFLAVONE chrysoeriol| to |FRAME: CPD-12571 selgin| was also demonstrated using microsomes from yeast expressing the |FRAME: G-58315 CYP75B4| gene |CITS: [26082402]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="MONOMER-20525" />
