    <DataNode elementId="MONOMER-20527" textLabel="flavonoid 3&apos;-monooxygenase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q7G602" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="841.1956176757812" centerY="1120.0489501953125" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="SRI, caspi">The |FRAME: G-58317 CYP75B3| gene of rice was considered a candidate for encoding |FRAME: EC-1.14.14.82 EC 1.14.14.82, flavonoid 3&amp;prime;-monooxygenase|, based on its homology to well-characterized ortholog from sorghum (82.8% identitiy). The gene was PCR-amplified from a cDNA clone and transformed into an Arabidopsis tt7 mutants, which are defective in this function, for complementation analysis. Transgenic tt7 mutants accumulate |FRAME: CPD1F-90 kaempferol| as the major flavonol, but the recombinant strain over-expressing the rice gene accumulated |FRAME: CPD-520 quercetin| as the major flavonol, indicating that |FRAME: G-58317 CYP75B3| encodes an |FRAME: EC-1.14.14.82 EC 1.14.14.82, flavonoid 3&amp;prime;-monooxygenase| |CITS: [18726614]|.</Comment>
