    <DataNode elementId="MONOMER-17890" textLabel="flavone synthase I" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="MONOMER-17890" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="745.9051513671875" centerY="869.0743408203125" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="O-28, hartmut">Utilizing the sequence of the |FRAME:TAX-4043 &lt;i&gt;Petroselinum crispum&lt;/i&gt;| flavone synthase I the TIGR rice index was screened and a gene (FNS I-1) encoding a rice flavone synthase I identified. The cDNA was cloned, expressed in |FRAME:TAX-562 &lt;i&gt;Escherichia coli&lt;/i&gt;| and the protein purified to homogeneity. The flavone synthase I catalyzed efficiently the introduction of the double bond (C2-C3) to the flavanone |FRAME:NARINGENIN-CMPD (&lt;i&gt;S&lt;/i&gt;)-naringenin| producing the flavone |FRAME:CPD-431 apigenin| in the process. The |FRAME:CPD-14042 (&lt;i&gt;R&lt;/i&gt;)-naringenin| was only converted at 13% of the catalytic activity of |FRAME:NARINGENIN-CMPD (&lt;i&gt;S&lt;/i&gt;)-naringenin|. The FNS I-1 from rice is the first flavone synthase I characterized outside the |FRAME:TAX-4037 &lt;i&gt;Apiaceae&lt;/i&gt;| family |CITS:[18304453]|.</Comment>
